---
system: sys-02-device-provisioning-registry
flow_id: transfer
surface: mobile
spec_anchor: /software/systems/02-device-provisioning-registry#transfer-request-status
actors: [SourceParentApp, TargetParentApp, Gateway, DeviceService, Device, PostgreSQL, TransferWorker]
apis:
  - POST /v1/devices/:deviceId/transfer/start
externals: []
queues: [devices.transitions]
failure_paths:
  - not_owner_role
  - device_busy_pending_ota
  - transfer_already_in_progress
  - target_claim_failed
  - transfer_broken_midway
idempotency: one active device_transfer_requests row per device (request_status not in terminal set)
retry: parent app retries on 5xx with exponential backoff
timeout: 5s p99 per endpoint
status: final
---
%% HAND-CURATED.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant SourceParentApp
    participant TargetParentApp
    participant Gateway
    participant DeviceService
    participant Device
    participant PostgreSQL
    participant TransferWorker

    SourceParentApp->>Gateway: POST /v1/devices/:deviceId/transfer/start (Parent bearer token, role=owner)
    Gateway->>DeviceService: forward
    alt not_owner_role
        DeviceService-->>SourceParentApp: 403 not_owner_role
    else device_busy_pending_ota
        DeviceService-->>SourceParentApp: 409 device_busy_pending_ota
    else transfer_already_in_progress
        DeviceService-->>SourceParentApp: 409 transfer_already_in_progress
    else success
        DeviceService->>PostgreSQL: INSERT device_transfer_requests {request_status=requested} then UPDATE devices.lifecycle_state='transfer_pending'
        PostgreSQL-->>DeviceService: transferRequestId
        DeviceService-->>SourceParentApp: 200 {transferRequestId, status=awaiting_factory_reset}
    end

    Note over Device,TransferWorker: source device factory-resets locally (out-of-band — sys-03 DECOMMISSIONED path)
    Device->>Gateway: POST /v1/device/provisioning/status {status=failed, reason=factory_reset}
    Gateway->>DeviceService: forward → enqueue devices.transitions.complete_transfer_after_reset

    TransferWorker->>PostgreSQL: SELECT device_transfer_requests WHERE request_status='awaiting_factory_reset'
    TransferWorker->>PostgreSQL: txn — close active device_ownership_history (ended_at, ownership_status='transferred'), UPDATE devices SET current_household_id=NULL lifecycle_state='unassigned' status='factory_new', UPDATE device_transfer_requests SET request_status='awaiting_target_claim'

    TargetParentApp->>Gateway: POST /v1/devices/provision/start {serialNumber} (target household)
    Note over TargetParentApp,PostgreSQL: continues via consumer-provisioning.sequence.mmd
    alt target_claim_failed
        DeviceService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE device_transfer_requests SET request_status='failed', failure_code
    else success
        DeviceService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE device_transfer_requests SET request_status='completed', completed_at
    end

    Note over Device,TransferWorker: transfer_broken_midway — integrity job detects (ownership not closed after reset) → freeze transfer_pending + support alert
    Note over SourceParentApp,PostgreSQL: timeout 5s p99 · transfer state machine per spec §7.4 · audit emit per mutation
